  "6f36ea2b-b350-4932-a301-703faf9a542f"],
 " use when none is given."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c0cbd234-7caa-490b-91ca-054adf0033a4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A scalar multiple has the degree of what it multiplies, a power ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", 
    StyleBox["g", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f09decc-db99-4270-9f05-831f2ad48363"],
 " has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba9089dd-9609-4b07-ad8c-3cccbf3b03f7"],
 " times the degree of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["HBar"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/HBar", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e9b941b3-e407-4baf-893d-bf164b1a518d"],
 ", and a sum has a degree when all its terms have the same one."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a56a604e-8867-4a32-8f2f-5b9738e27c37"],

Cell["\<\
A scalar multiple of a particle counts only when the scalar contains no \
particle.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"dd172da1-9aee-4751-8256-ee3cf1686d3f"],

Cell["\<\
The particles of the dual alphabet of a pairing object have their degrees too.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c5807793-7732-48d5-a90e-230dc18cbcd2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the bar grading ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 " may also be an association from particles to degrees."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ea125012-a747-4e98-b5b7-dd33e2cd8cbb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A sum of mixed degree, ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9f6df50d-2ba3-4625-b6b5-25f69e5a7c07"],
